@user-16 I like the explicit policy, my one worry is keeping it out of the public API. A per operation mode argument adds params across many call sites and a concept every user has to learn, which is a lot for a library this lean.

For almost every op the right policy is just "exact when richer geometry is present", which is already the de facto behavior (0.29.0 made `with_nms` and `area` OBB aware). I would keep that as the default and move the decision into one internal geometry resolution helper, so new ops route through it instead of re-deriving from `xyxy` and silently falling back. `EXACT` vs `ENVELOPE` still matters, but as an internal choice at the few ambiguous sites, not a global enum.

For enforcement, alongside your identical envelope fixtures, a metamorphic test fits well: rotate the detections off axis and require an exact op to give the same NMS keep set and `area`, both rotation invariant on OBB or mask geometry but not on the envelope. One property covers the whole cla
